From 864c7e3a81d67e5e7bc3e71a32b90b344e92ae2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jeeshofone <will.laws@me.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:31:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(channels): use the system proxy for the Slack Web API and
 Telegram

The Slack websocket and the gateway's aiohttp calls pick their proxy with
http_proxy.resolve_proxy, which on Windows falls back to the registry
through urllib.request.getproxies. The slack_sdk Web API clients were
built with no proxy, so they read the environment only, and Telegram's
resolver did the same. On a Windows host whose only egress is the system
proxy, the two legs of one channel took different routes.

Pass proxy=resolve_proxy(SLACK_API_URL) at every slack_sdk client the
gateway builds, and let Telegram fall back to resolve_proxy when no proxy
variable is set. Nothing is exported to kiro-cli or any other child. The
shared bypass check now matches host and host:port, and no longer raises
on an out-of-range port.

Fixes #34152
